    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Darlington-Campus/Building-Quality-Inspector_0155734-1": {
      "title": "Building Quality Inspector",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time, 2 years fixed term position. Located at the Services Building (G12) on the Darlington Campus Ensure the successful delivery of major infrastructure projects at the University of Sydney Competitive salary package on offer including 17% Superannuation About the opportunity The University of Sydney is welcoming applications for an experienced and motivated Building Quality Inspector to join the Infrastructure Delivery team. The Building Quality Inspector (BQI) plays a critical role in the successful delivery of major infrastructure projects at the University of Sydney. Acting as the University’s on-site representative, the BQI provides independent oversight of construction activities to ensure the highest standards of quality, safety, and compliance are maintained throughout project delivery. The role is responsible for monitoring construction works against approved designs, specifications, relevant standards, and regulatory requirements. Through rigorous inspections, documentation, and reporting, the BQI identifies and addresses potential issues early, minimises defects and rework, protects project integrity, and supports the delivery of high-quality outcomes that provide long-term value for the University. The Building Quality Inspector (BQI) will work closely with project teams, contractors, and key stakeholders to ensure construction activities are delivered safely, efficiently, and to the required standards of quality and compliance. The successful candidate will be based on-site and responsible for overseeing construction projects across the University of Sydney’s Darlington and Camperdown campuses. Your key responsibilities will be to: conduct daily inspections of construction activities to ensure compliance with design specifications, engineering drawings, and quality standards monitor the quality of workmanship and materials used, identifying any deviations or substandard practices verify that all construction activities comply with relevant building codes, statutory regulations, and University policies conduct safety inspections and identify potential hazards, unsafe practices, or non-compliant equipment. detect and document construction defects or poor workmanship early in the process to prevent rework and delays provide clear, concise, and timely updates to the Project Director to support informed decision-making review construction drawings, specifications, and technical documents to ensure clarity and feasibility engage with contractors to understand their three-week lookahead schedules and prepare for upcoming inspections. About you accredited/licensed building trade qualification or an equivalent combination of relevant training and experience minimum 20 years of relevant experience in building construction, quality assurance, and regulatory compliance proven track record in site inspection, defect identification, and construction oversight experience working with diverse trades on complex infrastructure projects in major-level health, research or education buildings working knowledge of WHS responsibilities and risk management, obligations and applying SafeWork NSW legislation & regulation into the workplace extensive knowledge of regulatory requirements in the building industry (including NSW Legislation, BCA, Australian Standards) as well as technical knowledge of professional disciplines effective communication skills (both verbal and written) with ability to interact, influence and negotiate with a broad range of people within and outside the University with a high level of tact, diplomacy, and discretion, including the ability to manage people who may be in distress or difficulty deep understanding of construction inspection processes and quality assurance. Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to be eligible to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks and declarations  Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page. Please address the “about you” section in your cover letter with relevant examples. For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Kevin Lim, Recruitment Operations by email to kevin.lim@sydney.edu.au . © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Tuesday 15 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
